From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jan <1760229+slomin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 02:09:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] cpu: the delta-net writes its state into the cache, the copy
 skipped; concat split by rows (#190)

The CPU counterpart of #185's Metal delta-net write-back. The fused
GATED_DELTA_NET puts its new recurrent state after its output and the graph
copies it into the cache, 2 MB per layer for Millie. A per-graph plan finds
each such copy (a plain F32 copy of exactly that range, nothing between the
two nodes touching either range, nothing else ever reading the state); the op
then writes its state straight into the cache, skips its own input copy when
that is the same place, and the copy node is skipped. VIEW-like nodes read
nothing themselves, so they don't count as readers. The same values land in
the same place.

CONCAT split its work over ne2, which is 1 for decode's conv_input, so one
thread copied 8192 rows while four waited; it now splits over rows.

12R tg128, two interleaved rounds: 13.78 with the write-back off
(MILLIE_GDN_WB=0), 14.39 on.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu-impl.h b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu-impl.h
index 5d1ca5f..5b566e9 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu-impl.h
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu-impl.h
@@ -27,6 +27,10 @@ struct ggml_compute_params {
 
     // use reference implementation
     bool use_ref;
+
+    // #190: GATED_DELTA_NET writes its new state here instead of into its own
+    // result, when the graph's copy of that state into the cache was folded in
+    void * state_dst;
 };
 
 
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c
index 15504e8..f11791b 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c
